# oracle: pair_style edip (Si.edip) on a displaced diamond Si 2x2x2 cell with a vacancy (delete_atoms), 100 steps of nve from variable velocities
# oracle-potentials: Si.edip
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=2e-6 abs=1e-6
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): on this case native edip/multi reading the same Si.edip gives press -644.369072008205 at step 0, equal to the engine (-644.3690720082104), while native edip gives -644.368549221789; native's single-element style departs from the analytic EDIP form by about 1e-6 in pressure and 3e-9 in energy, so the single-element cases use rel 2e-6
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify     map array
boundary        p p p
atom_modify     sort 0 0.0
variable        a equal 5.431
lattice         custom $a a1 1.0 0.0 0.0 a2 0.0 1.0 0.0 a3 0.0 0.0 1.0 &
                basis 0.0 0.0 0.0 basis 0.0 0.5 0.5 basis 0.5 0.0 0.5 basis 0.5 0.5 0.0 &
                basis 0.25 0.25 0.25 basis 0.25 0.75 0.75 basis 0.75 0.25 0.75 basis 0.75 0.75 0.25
region          myreg block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box      1 myreg
create_atoms    1 region myreg
mass            1 28.06
variable        dx atom 0.04*sin(1.3*x+0.7*y)
variable        dy atom 0.04*cos(0.9*y-0.4*z)
variable        dz atom 0.04*sin(1.1*z+0.5*x)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
group           del id 30
delete_atoms    group del
variable        vx atom 0.01*sin(id)
variable        vy atom 0.01*cos(2*id)
variable        vz atom 0.01*sin(3*id)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz
pair_style      edip
pair_coeff      * * Si.edip Si
timestep        1.0e-3
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 10 check yes
thermo_style    custom step pe press etotal
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          10
fix             1 all nve
run             100
